WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:35.440
<b>"Idol Festival" 2014</b>

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.650
It's an application form 
for the Idol Festival.

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:36.350
You will be entering this.

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:37.990
What?!

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:41.640
Anyway, master this song.

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:48.840
It's your new song, "First Rate Smile."

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.000
I wrote it for you.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:56.720
<b>Goal: Major Debut!!</b>

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.340
If you're going to be singing my songs,

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:56.720
the school festival feel 
you've been bringing won't cut it.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:58.650
See you later.

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:00.220
Make sure you learn the song 
by the next time I see you.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:06.390
<b>"Idol Festival" 2014</b>

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.390
An idol festival?

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.560
G-Good morning.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.420
Good work on your daily lessons.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.580
As you all know,

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:43.600
the I-1 Club National 47 Prefecture 
Love Connection Project

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.180
will meet its goal

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:49.400
of opening a theater in every 
prefecture by the end of the year.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:53.100
But it's far too early to relax.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.940
The battle is only just beginning.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.150
The Idol Festival!

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:03.950
This year, you'll face the idol 
groups across the country you've been

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:07.950
competing with on I-1's home turf, Tokyo.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:11.900
Those who make it through 
their local preliminaries

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.330
will challenge us at the end of the year.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:17.350
Of course, you won't 
compete with them directly.

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:19.380
However, standing on the 
same stage with them

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.470
is the same as battling them.

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:26.970
You will engage them, take them down, 
and crush them to smithereens!

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:35.730
Oh, and numbers 1135, 1136, and 1137.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.440
Y-Yes!

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.990
You greeted me just now 
when I entered the room.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.090
Yes!

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.800
Are you stupid?

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:45.960
Listen carefully.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:48.220
The battlefield extends beyond the stage.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:50.250
It even applies to your lessons.

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:53.850
Let your guard down even a little, 
and you're finished.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:58.090
Once you stand here, 
pay no attention to anything else.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.260
Focus solely on your singing and dancing.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:04.670
Nothing captures the hearts 
of fans more than focus.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:06.150
We're sorry!

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:07.760
There are no second chances.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:11.660
Anyway, it's time for 
the usual announcements.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:19.780
189, 490, 795, 864, 1003, and 1129.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.900
Good bye to the six of you.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.030
Don't come back, starting tomorrow.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:28.890
In this age of warring idols, 
we must protect our position of power.

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:31.780
Let us conclude this day by singing

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:33.140
the necessary attributes 
of a popular idol together.

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:33.760
Yes!

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:36.600
Don't rest! Don't complain! Don't think!

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:39.670
Don't rest! Don't complain! Don't think!

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.050
Always gratitude!

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.800
Always gratitude!

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:56.270
I think I can finally like idols.

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:03.520
Mai, let's do it one more time.

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:04.270
Okay.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:06.570
Let's practice our basics one more time!

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:07.800
Yes!

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:10.080
What? Hayasaka-san is?

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:15.330
Yeah. I heard he's producing that 
Sendai group Shimada Mayu's in.

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:19.270
They must be amazing if 
Hayasaka-san has his eye on them.

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:24.450
But isn't Wake Up, Girls! from 
a really small and weak agency?

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:25.850
I'm surprised they could afford him.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:27.250
It's not like that.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:29.800
Hayasaka-san is the one 
who was interested in them.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:32.130
Really? Go figure.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.030
Should you be impressed?

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:36.090
During our opening concert in Sendai,

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:40.010
he went to see a Wake Up, Girls! 
concert and asked to produce them...

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:42.450
For free, if you'd believe it.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.980
You're kidding! That money-grubber?

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:46.990
It must not be about the money.

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:51.120
But what's Shiraki-san going to do?

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.120
<b>Track 13

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:05.770
There are some parts that bother me, 
but it's mostly okay.

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:07.130
I see.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:11.390
Anyway, how is Wake Up, Girls! doing?

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:14.140
Oh? You already heard about that?

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:17.480
Long ago. Even my girls know about it.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:19.130
How terrifying.

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:22.350
The walls have ears, 
and the doors have eyes.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:25.490
Well, you can't have too many rivals.

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:29.670
If you're always leading the pack, 
your times will never improve.

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:32.220
It's the blues of being the top runner.

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:34.150
I thought you'd say that.

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:37.040
Shimada Mayu is good, isn't she?

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.420
What?

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:42.670
Oh, it's certainly no wonder 
she was I-1's first center.

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:47.320
If she pulls the other 
amateur members along,

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:51.170
Wake Up, Girls! might end up 
being an interesting group.

00:06:51.170 --> 00:06:52.680
I don't know about that.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.870
Do you really think she can do that?

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:58.660
Anyway, the Idol Festival is 
excited by the simple fact

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:01.620
of Shimada Mayu's participation.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:03.940
Isn't that good news for you?

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:05.510
I suppose.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:09.950
Let's just say I'm doing 
Wake Up, Girls! a favor by sending you.

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:14.200
A favor? That's some favor 
you're doing for them.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.740
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.740
Is this for real? It's amazing!

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:23.000
<b>Idol Festival</b>

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:21.030
Yeah. Apparently, idols from all over Japan

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:23.000
gather and compete to be the best.

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:26.160
It started three years ago.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.890
It's like the Local Mascot Contest.

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:31.120
Don't compare this to that.

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:33.140
Don't make fun of local mascots.

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:38.300
The winners of each region 
get to participate in the finals

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:40.390
held at the end of the year in the I-1 Arena!

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:43.850
What? You mean <i>that</i> I-1 Arena?

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:44.910
Isn't that amazing?

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:48.210
It's like a super version of the 
most amazing thing you can think of.

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:49.730
It's super-duper amazing.

00:07:49.730 --> 00:07:52.070
It's the holy ground of idols.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:52.780
What?

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:57.780
And the winner gets 
a contract with Queen Records!

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:01.170
You mean <i>that</i> Queen Records?

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:04.750
It's practically a Cinderella story!

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.300
I'm so excited!

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.280
If we can make our break here,

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:10.800
we'll be able to pay off 
the rest of our debts!

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:12.580
I found the perfect place.

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:14.540
It'd be just right for our new office building.

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:15.550
I'm going to go check it out.

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:18.080
Huh? What?

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:18.930
President?

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:21.610
She's being a little hasty.

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:24.940
I was just speaking 
hypothetically if we won.

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:26.060
We can do it.

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:32.070
Only if I do my best, though.

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:34.700
But I <i>will</i> do my best.

00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:38.230
Let's give it a try.

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:38.920
Yeah.

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:41.620
They do say participating 
bears great significance.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.460
That's what they say 
about the Olympics.

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:45.920
Tokyo has hosted the Olympics before.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.960
Yeah, sure. Whatever.

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:52.370
Hayasaka-san's busy with I-1 
performances for a few weeks,

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:53.970
so he won't be able to come here.

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:59.150
The official word is you should 
master this song by your next lesson.

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:01.180
He gave us the choreography, too.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:02.580
I spoke with your dance instructor

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:05.040
so you can begin practicing right away.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:07.410
Learn the choreography by tomorrow.

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:08.550
Okay!

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:10.480
Do you girls have a minute?

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.600
What?

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:13.230
Do you want to go get something to eat?

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:17.610
Sure, but you don't usually 
invite everyone out.

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:19.460
You think so?

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:22.770
Deepening our friendship isn't 
so bad once in a while, right?

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:24.620
If you still don't want to go, 
I'd be willing to pay.

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:25.790
Let's go.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:26.940
Where do you want to go?

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:29.060
Should we go to my workplace?

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:30.850
That place is too expensive.

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:33.240
But you have my discount.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:34.170
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:38.390
What about the pancake 
house we covered before?

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:39.670
Oh, "Honeybee"?

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:43.020
Yeah. They've even got 
ten-layer pancakes.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:44.980
They're really good.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:46.310
Let's go there, then.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:49.410
I need to talk to Matsuda-san.

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:50.400
I'll catch up later.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:51.730
What? With me?

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:52.320
Yes.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:57.490
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:55.060
We'll go on ahead, then, Nanami.

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:56.740
We'll be waiting for you, Nanami.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:57.490
Okay.

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:01.030
Anyway, this song seems difficult.

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:03.290
We'll be practicing like crazy, 
starting tomorrow.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:06.710
We need to put something together 
by the time he comes back.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:07.910
That's right.

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:10.290
Let's surprise him with our progress.

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:12.790
So, what did you want 
to talk to me about?

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:15.800
<b>Certain Victory: Idol Festival!!</b>

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:17.300
<b>Hikarizuka Music School</b>

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:17.300
This is...

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:37.820
<b>Certain Victory: Idol Festival!!</b>

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:21.030
Now that I think of it, you mentioned 
this during your audition.

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:24.040
Yes. They're the entrance 
requirements for Hikarizuka.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:26.320
I'm thinking I should 
start focusing on studying

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:27.640
for the entrance exam soon.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.360
What? But...

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:31.580
The entrance exam is next spring.

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:34.970
I had always intended to stop 
working with WUG by then.

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:36.420
Huh? What?

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:37.830
What?!

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:42.450
Anyway, I won't be able 
to participate in the Idol Festival.

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:44.580
What? What?!

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:46.580
I'm sorry.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:48.710
Anyway, I hope you understand.

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.030
What?

00:10:50.030 --> 00:10:51.290
Excuse me.

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:53.170
Hey, wait...

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:54.840
Um...

00:10:57.970 --> 00:10:59.070
What am I going to do?

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:00.720
Nanami!

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:02.470
President?

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:05.190
What? What's with the slack expression?

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:06.810
That's not important!

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:07.720
It's an emergency!

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.230
What?

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:11.600
Minami-chan, it's been a while.

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:15.480
After you came, we were covered 
by a bunch of other places.

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:19.210
It's all because you made 
the food look so good.

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:22.020
But the food really is good.

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:26.940
Today, we even have people 
from I-1 coming to cover the place.

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:27.520
What?

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.920
They should be arriving soon.

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:31.620
Hello!

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.240
Welcome.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:35.630
Thank you for having us today.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.300
I'm their manager, Machida.

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:38.380
What are you doing here, Mayu?

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:38.380
Nice to meet you.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.890
It's nice to meet you, too.

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:56.110
Should we address it to Honeybee?

00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:57.430
Oh, well.

00:11:57.430 --> 00:12:00.900
Just when I thought we'd 
established a place for WUG fans...

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:04.170
It feels like I-1 stole it 
right out from under us.

00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:05.650
We can't help it.

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:09.060
They have theaters operating 
all over the country.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:12.450
But we're the ones who get 
to live in the area and

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:13.920
come here all the time.

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:22.700
Whoa! The I-1 center is coming this way!

00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:26.490
Hayasaka-san is strict, isn't he?

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:27.100
Huh?

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:29.240
Yeah, he is.

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:34.810
But he's not interested 
in hopeless individuals.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:36.560
Thanks for waiting.

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:38.520
Look at that.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:39.570
What's going on?

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:42.570
She wanted to talk about 
something and dragged her away.

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:44.870
What are they talking about?

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:46.320
Their past, maybe?

00:12:46.940 --> 00:12:49.870
Mayushi, you're as cute as ever.

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:52.700
But, Shihocchi, your skin is so smooth.

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:53.800
Like that?

00:12:53.800 --> 00:12:54.790
No way.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.040
I wonder if Mayushi's okay.

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:58.610
I'll handle it, if I have to.

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:00.000
What are you? A hit man?

00:13:02.020 --> 00:13:05.480
I heard you're participating 
in the Idol Festival, too.

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:06.130
Yeah.

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:10.390
Don't forget you used to be part of I-1.

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:11.540
What?

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:13.690
If you're just going to 
produce embarrassing results,

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:15.740
it's better not to participate at all.

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:18.070
You'll damage I-1's reputation.

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:21.190
If you're coming, bring everything you have.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:22.980
I'll crush you will all I've got.

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:29.290
Thank you for today.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:30.360
No. Thank you.

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:32.360
Please come again.

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:37.820
Are you all right?

00:13:37.820 --> 00:13:39.750
Did she say anything mean?

00:13:41.140 --> 00:13:42.500
What did she say to you?

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:45.260
It wasn't anything special.

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:49.730
Our pancakes are getting cold over there.

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:51.000
Poor pancakes.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.010
You're right. Sorry.

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:55.020
<b>It's happening again this year! 
The battle to determine the nation's greatest idol, the Idol Festival. 
This year marks the fourth time the nation's greatest idol will be chosen. 
The winning group will be officially recognized as I-1's rival and will make their major debut and receive a one-year contract.</b>

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:55.020
"Idol Festival 2014"

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:58.460
<b>I'm so excited for the center battle!</b>

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:01.520
<b>I'm amazed Shimada's brazenly working as an idol. 
WUG brought in Hayasaka for help! 
Who knows what will happen now?</b>

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:04.190
<i>I can't help that WUG is</i>

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:07.730
<i>compared to I-1 and criticized 
with Mayushi in their roster.</i>

00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:11.530
<i>However, I hope WUG ignores 
such comments and grows</i>

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:13.990
<i>in their own way at their own pace.</i>

00:14:14.390 --> 00:14:17.500
Regional preliminary idol predictions?

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:21.970
Hokkaido's Puchi Marimo, 
Nagoya's Akamiso All-stars,

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:24.000
and Osaka's Team Cheetah 
are sure things.

00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:28.210
However, everyone's focused 
on the dark horse,

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:31.510
former I-1 center's 
Wake Up, Girls!...

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:34.310
It wouldn't be impossible 
for us to win!

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:35.880
To win?

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:37.430
Let me see that!

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:38.270
Me, too!

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:41.220
If we win, we'll make 
our mainstream debut.

00:14:41.220 --> 00:14:43.410
It'll be our big break.

00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:45.860
We'll be on the covers 
of all kinds of magazines.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:49.450
We might even appear on music 
shows on Tokyo TV stations.

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:53.090
And at the end of the year, 
the Red vs. White Concert...

00:14:53.090 --> 00:14:56.010
We've got to do it!

00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:58.920
WUG's time is coming!

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:00.770
You have a basic grasp 
of the choreography, right?

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:01.420
Yes!

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:03.420
Give it a try, then.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:04.040
Okay!

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:07.060
That's all for today.

00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:09.790
Fix your problem areas by tomorrow.

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:10.530
Okay!

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:12.300
Thank you very much!

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:14.430
1, 2, 3, 4...

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:15.850
5, 6, 7, 8.

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:18.360
You're not accenting your movements.

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:19.060
It's like this.

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:20.850
1, 2, 3, 4...

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:22.860
5, 6, 7, 8.

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:24.310
Okay.

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:26.350
Give it another try.

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:27.110
Okay.

00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:29.370
1, 2, 3, 4...

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:29.860
Huh?

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:31.060
That's not it.

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:31.860
Watch carefully.

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:33.620
1, 2, 3, 4...

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:35.610
5, 6, 7, 8.

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:36.870
Okay.

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:38.620
1, 2, 3, 4...

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:39.750
That's not right!

00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:43.220
I'm sorry.

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:45.970
I'm out.

00:15:45.970 --> 00:15:47.560
I'm thirsty, too.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:49.740
Do you want me to get some for you?

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:50.510
Sure.

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:54.390
Why don't you two take a break, too?

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:56.320
But we need to practice a little more.

00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:58.520
Don't you think you're working too hard?

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:01.520
When I was part of I-1, we practiced more.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:03.270
Why would you say that?

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:05.010
It's okay.

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:07.860
I asked Mayu to teach me.

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:09.570
It's late.

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:12.050
Why don't you stop for today 
and pick things up tomorrow?

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:17.590
I'm going to stay and keep practicing.

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:19.540
You girls can go ahead.

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:22.310
Mayushi, I hope you'll 
teach me again tomorrow.

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:25.460
I'll stay, too.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:26.540
Huh?

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:32.620
Do you want to stop by 
Honeybee again today?

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:33.880
Sounds good.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:35.490
I'm hungry.

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:36.560
What about you, Mayushi.

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:38.300
I'm going home.

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:45.270
1, 2, 3, 4...

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.060
5, 6, 7, 8.

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:48.920
1, 2, 3, 4...

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:50.570
5, 6, 7, 8.

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:52.890
1, 2, 3, 4...

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:54.320
1, 2, 3, 4...

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:56.710
5, 6, 7, 8.

00:16:57.850 --> 00:16:58.780
What do you think?

00:16:59.270 --> 00:17:01.590
You're most of the way there.

00:17:01.590 --> 00:17:03.650
But you need to stick your heel out

00:17:03.650 --> 00:17:07.120
farther for the last part, like this.

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:09.220
Okay. Like this?

00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:10.800
Yeah, that's it.

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:14.300
You know, you don't usually stay late.

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:17.050
Huh? Oh, yeah...

00:17:18.070 --> 00:17:20.110
What a difficult song.

00:17:20.110 --> 00:17:21.940
I need to practice more.

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:25.410
You're lucky you can do it properly.

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:28.190
I need to work even harder.

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:31.500
I don't want to hold 
everyone back anymore.

00:17:32.370 --> 00:17:33.990
Can I ask you something?

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:35.070
What?

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:37.740
How can you work so hard?

00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:38.850
Huh?

00:17:39.860 --> 00:17:42.990
Because I've been given this chance.

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:47.000
After discussing it, we decided 
we'd do anything to bring you back!

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:50.590
I don't want to let them down, 
and I don't want to run away.

00:17:51.230 --> 00:17:52.630
Huh...

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:58.660
Since I was little I've never 
been good at anything I've tried.

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:00.160
I could never keep anything up.

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:02.640
I always ended up quitting right away.

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:07.520
But after everything that happened, 
I gave it some thought.

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:09.650
I decided I wanted to change who I am.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:12.210
That's why I auditioned for WUG.

00:18:12.210 --> 00:18:15.510
I decided that if I got in, I'd do my best

00:18:15.510 --> 00:18:18.240
instead of running, 
for once in my life, but...

00:18:20.060 --> 00:18:22.160
But nothing changed.

00:18:22.770 --> 00:18:24.830
I was still holding everyone back.

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:26.250
I ran away.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:33.550
I knew that wasn't good enough, 
but my feelings were half-hearted.

00:18:34.470 --> 00:18:36.010
Half-hearted...

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:39.400
I'm a huge WUG fan.

00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:41.460
I really love them.

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:44.560
I don't think I could love anything more.

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:51.690
That's why I wanted to be a proper 
member instead of just a fan.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:57.160
Right now, my head's full 
of thoughts about the Idol Festival.

00:18:57.160 --> 00:18:59.950
I'll do anything to win.

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:01.950
I see.

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:18.090
Okay, stop.

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:21.090
You're barely scoring twenty points.

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:23.850
But we're doing our best.

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:26.220
Doing your best? What?

00:19:26.550 --> 00:19:28.340
That's normal!

00:19:28.340 --> 00:19:30.080
Everyone's working hard!

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:31.940
What's important is producing results!

00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:35.770
In order to do that, you need 
to work two, three, four, ten,

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:37.660
a hundred times harder 
than everyone else!

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:39.190
How many hours did you 
practice this week?

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:43.360
A little more than twenty, I think.

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:44.550
So few!

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:46.340
That's not nearly enough!

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:48.870
That's not even half 
the time I-1 practiced!

00:19:51.430 --> 00:19:54.850
Well, it's not as though just 
practicing for more hours is enough.

00:19:54.850 --> 00:19:56.410
You have to work a hundred times as hard

00:19:56.410 --> 00:19:59.340
and produce a thousand times the results.

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:00.720
See you next week.

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:07.910
At this rate, you won't make 
it out of the preliminaries.

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:11.950
He didn't have to put it that way.

00:20:11.950 --> 00:20:14.170
Do you think it's impossible, after all?

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:16.130
That can't be true.

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:19.030
He said we didn't practice 
half as much as I-1.

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:21.790
That means we're not 
practicing nearly enough.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:24.530
Let's call it quits for today and...

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:25.530
Wait, Yoppi.

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:30.540
I do think we don't practice enough.

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:35.790
Like Hayasaka-san said, 
I-1's lessons aren't nearly this easy.

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:41.050
We should practice more 
effectively and more earnestly.

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:43.290
At this rate, I really do think

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:45.390
our chances in the preliminaries are shady.

00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:48.190
We should review everything 
from our lesson plans

00:20:48.190 --> 00:20:49.310
to the time we spend.

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:51.370
Mayushi, you're just flustered.

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:52.060
Of course I am!

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:56.020
I'm saying these half-hearted 
practices aren't good enough.

00:20:56.340 --> 00:20:58.400
We can't beat the I-1 Club like this!

00:20:58.760 --> 00:20:59.150
What?

00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:02.550
Why do you keep bringing them up?

00:21:02.550 --> 00:21:04.150
The I-1 Club has nothing to do with us!

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:08.420
I don't know what the I-1 center said to you,

00:21:08.420 --> 00:21:13.190
but you said you were working 
with WUG to make yourself happy.

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:15.790
Does that mean beating the I-1 Club?

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:18.640
I don't know why you quit I-1,

00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:21.670
but why do you have to drag us into it?

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:23.170
That's not what I meant.

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:24.250
What, then?

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:27.040
You're always dodging 
our questions when it comes to this!

00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:29.470
Huh? What's going on?

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:31.220
Why did you quit?

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:34.350
Why don't you just tell us the truth already?

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:35.100
Hey!

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:36.270
That has nothing to do with this!

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:37.270
It does!

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:39.110
Stop!

00:21:42.310 --> 00:21:43.230
Mayu!

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:46.780
Mayu?

00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:59.290
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:21:55.740 --> 00:21:56.920
An overnight trip?

00:21:56.920 --> 00:21:59.290
Yes, Kaya suggested it.

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:03.260
But is it really all right 
to go under those conditions?

00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:08.090
It'd be good for them 
to let off some steam.

00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:09.680
For real, this time.

00:22:10.420 --> 00:22:13.310
President, the group 
is in danger of collapsing!

00:22:13.310 --> 00:22:14.890
To be continued

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:47.420
<b>Episode Preview</b>

00:23:45.350 --> 00:23:47.420
Kayatan, you're the sub-leader, right?

00:23:47.420 --> 00:23:48.100
That's right.

00:23:48.100 --> 00:23:49.900
What does the sub-leader do?

00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:51.440
What do I do?

00:23:51.440 --> 00:23:53.510
I guess I support Yoppi.

00:23:53.510 --> 00:23:55.880
It doesn't mean you're 
the leader of the sub, right?

00:23:55.880 --> 00:23:57.520
Yeah, I don't know what that means.

00:23:57.520 --> 00:24:00.000
The next episode is 
"Living Here!"

00:23:57.680 --> 00:24:00.000
<b>"Living Here"</b>
